<title>USA: Chrysler files for $1.5 bln shelf offering.</title>
<headline>Chrysler files for $1.5 bln shelf offering.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp. filed on Tuesday with the Securities and Exchange Commission for a shelf offering of up to $1.5 billion of debentures.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes, the company said.</p>
<p>Underwriters for the sale are Salomon Brothers Inc., Chase Securities Inc., Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co., Merrill Lynch &amp; Co. and J.P. Morgan &amp; Co., it said.</p>
